<title>FRANCE: France's Lamassoure say dollar still undervalued.</title>
<headline>France's Lamassoure say dollar still undervalued.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French government spokesman Alain Lamassoure hailed on Wednesday the rise of the dollar against European currencies but said it remained undervalued.</p>
<p>&quot;It is true that the dollar is and remains undervalued against the major European currencies,&quot; Lamassore told Europe 1 radio.</p>
<p>At the same time, he said, &quot;We must rejoice that in a few days it (the dollar) has gone from five francs to 5.30 francs.&quot;</p>
<p>He added that the parity between the franc and the mark &quot;is good.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
